Error: Unknown option: --io-free
Usage:
  poison-interpreter --repl
  poison-interpreter [--verbose] [--regime "1=true"] [--extern-regime "238=true"] <file>
  poison-interpreter --help

Regime options (FR-aware typing of guarded externs):
  --extern-regime "id=bool"  Preferred. Selects externs by id; interprets every
                             output tag the typechecker allocates for that callable.
                             Robust against allocation order; does not reach
                             'extern val' declaration guards.
  --regime "k=bool"          Low-level, concrete-tag control. Names numeric guard
                             tags directly and is allocation-order dependent (tags
                             are numbered in typechecker traversal order from 1,
                             not strictly textual order). Use mainly for debugging
                             or guards --extern-regime cannot reach.

Exit Codes:
  0  Success (including successful detection of type errors)
  1  Usage error (wrong command-line arguments)
  2  Parse error (syntax error in source)
  3  AST construction error (internal parser error)
  4  Type checker out of fuel (analysis couldn't complete)
  5  File I/O error (can't read file)
  6  Runtime error (evaluation failed)
  7  Evaluation out of fuel (divergence)

Note: Exit code 0 indicates that the analysis tool itself worked correctly,
regardless of whether the program being analyzed is well-typed. This follows
the convention of compilers that return 0 even when reporting type errors,
since successfully finding errors is a success for the tool.
